Company Description
Job Description
We’re building the Go-To-Market team for Base44, an AI-powered software development platform recently acquired by Wix. In this role, you’ll be at the forefront of a category-defining shift in how software is built—bringing a transformative product to the SMB segments. This is a high-impact, high-velocity role for a seller who thrives in an entrepreneurial environment. You won’t just be following a playbook; you’ll be helping to write it. Working closely with Base44 and Wix leadership, you will drive the full sales cycle, turning technical innovation into tangible business value for our customers.
In your day-to-day, you will:
Manage the full sales cycle from aggressive outbound prospecting to closing high-growth SMB accounts&#xa0;&#xa0;
Turn Base44’s AI capabilities into "business-speak" that resonates with CXOs, Product Leads, and Founders&#xa0;&#xa0;
Shape the foundational sales motion, including messaging, outreach strategies, and customer segmentation to support future scale&#xa0;&#xa0;
Identify and convert high-potential prospects, building the early momentum that defines our market presence&#xa0;&#xa0;
Act as a critical feedback loop between the market and our product team to influence the roadmap and positioning&#xa0;&#xa0;
Maintain a clean CRM and provide accurate deal forecasting to support our rapid growth&#xa0;
Qualifications
5+ years of B2B sales experience in a technology company, with a proven track record of smashing quotas&#xa0;&#xa0;
Experience with shorter sales cycles and high-volume deal flow, particularly in SMB environments&#xa0;&#xa0;
Comfort discussing technical workflows, with experience in AI, ML, or developer-centric SaaS – an advantage&#xa0;&#xa0;
Self-motivated, goal-oriented, and comfortable with the ambiguity of a "startup within a giant" environment&#xa0;&#xa0;
Strong communication skills with the ability to tailor complex messaging to both technical and non-technical audiences&#xa0;
Additional Information
We're Base44, a newly acquired part of Wix, on a mission to redefine how software is built. Our AI-powered platform enables anyone to create custom software applications using natural language—no coding required. Operating like a startup within Wix, we're fast, collaborative, and focused on solving complex problems with simple, powerful solutions.&#xa0;&#xa0;
We exist to empower creators, solo founders, startups, entrepreneurs, and side hustlers to bring their ideas to life. Whether you're launching a product, validating a concept, or exploring a new idea, Base44 is here to help you build it.&#xa0;&#xa0;
We're growing rapidly, the potential is immense, and with your expertise, we can drive user-driven growth to new heights.

Company Description
Job Description
As Head of Security for Base44, you'll lead and implement security strategies, ensuring robust protection for our products, clients, and internal systems. With a dotted-line to the Wix CISO, you'll serve as Base44's primary security authority while ensuring full alignment with Wix's corporate security standards, policies, and enterprise-grade compliance requirements.
&#xa0;
In your day-to-day, you will:&#xa0;&#xa0;
&#xa0;
Design, architect, and implement security features directly into our product codebase&#xa0;&#xa0;
leading pre-sales security engagements meetings, executive security discussions, CISO-level reviews, and vendor security assessments while representing the company's security posture.&#xa0;&#xa0;
Set standards and best practices across R&D and product teams as the sole internal authority for security&#xa0;&#xa0;
Work closely with Wix CISO and the broader Wix Security departments to align Base44's security posture with corporate policies, compliance frameworks, and enterprise requirements
Qualifications
7+ years of hands-on security experience, specifically in product security or application security.
6+ years of experience in customer-facing roles, representing the company to client CISOs, IT directors, and security teams (Enterprise & SMB)&#xa0;&#xa0;
Strong understanding of cloud security (AWS/GCP/Azure), web application security (OWASP Top 10), and secure architecture design&#xa0;&#xa0;
Proven background in B2B SaaS companies&#xa0;&#xa0;
Ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment, balancing deep technical execution with high-level strategic and client discussions
Additional Information
We're Base44, a newly acquired part of Wix, on a mission to redefine how software is built. Our AI-powered platform enables anyone to create custom software applications using natural language—no coding required. Operating like a startup within Wix, we're fast, collaborative, and focused on solving complex problems with simple, powerful solutions.&#xa0;&#xa0;
We exist to empower creators, solo founders, startups, entrepreneurs, and side hustlers to bring their ideas to life. Whether you're launching a product, validating a concept, or exploring a new idea, Base44 is here to help you build it.&#xa0;&#xa0;
We're growing rapidly, the potential is immense, and with your expertise, we can drive user-driven growth to new heights.

Company Description
Job Description
As a Demand Generation Manager, you'll drive multi-channel demand programs, manage ABM strategies, and optimize conversion funnels to generate pipeline contribution and revenue influence. You'll work closely with sales and other teams to create and execute targeted campaigns while analyzing performance to ensure continuous improvement. You'll also collaborate with the Base44 B2C user acquisition team and creative team to create holistic and converting content and campaigns.
In your day-to-day, you will:&#xa0;
Own and execute multi-channel demand programs, running campaigns across paid, content syndication, and events targeting enterprise buyers&#xa0;
Lead ABM strategy and execution, identifying and tiering target accounts, coordinating with Sales, and running account-specific plays across platforms like LinkedIn and others&#xa0;
Manage the PLG-to-Enterprise conversion funnel, optimizing the path from self-serve sign-up to Sales-Qualified Accounts in collaboration with RevOps&#xa0;
Drive pipeline reporting and campaign analytics by building dashboards to track key metrics and inform decisions&#xa0;
Collaborate with Base44’s B2C user acquisition and creative teams to create holistic and converting content and campaigns&#xa0;
Work with cross-functional teams to ensure successful execution of demand generation strategies
Qualifications
2+ years in B2B demand generation or growth marketing at a SaaS company, with ownership of pipeline metrics&#xa0;&#xa0;
2+ years of experience working with a PLG product or a company transitioning from self-serve/freemium to enterprise sales&#xa0;&#xa0;
Practical experience with ABM tools like 6sense, Demandbase, or Terminus&#xa0;&#xa0;
Ability to independently build and optimize campaigns on LinkedIn Ads, Google Ads, and review platforms like G2 or Capterra&#xa0;&#xa0;
Strong skills in SQL or BI tools for custom reporting, with an understanding of multi-touch attribution models&#xa0;&#xa0;
Builder mentality, strategic and executional range, and strong collaboration and communication skills&#xa0;&#xa0;
Additional Information
We are Base44’s Marketing Team. We’re the face of Base44, driving business growth, user optimization, and brand awareness. We’re a dynamic, dedicated, and fun group that plays a crucial role in Base44’s marketing efforts, introducing new and existing clients to our incredible suite of services. We collaborate and communicate across multiple channels, helping businesses and organizations achieve their goals and succeed online.&#xa0;

Company Description
Job Description
As a Motion Designer at Base44, you'll craft compelling visual narratives through motion, built on a strong foundation of design principles. You'll design for motion using composition, typography, and color, ensuring that movement naturally extends the brand’s visual identity and storytelling. In your day-to-day, you will:&#xa0;&#xa0;
Develop styleframes and storyboards to establish the creative direction for projects&#xa0;&#xa0;
Shape brand aesthetics through motion, ensuring consistency across digital platforms&#xa0;&#xa0;
Collaborate with designers, animators, editors, and 3D artists to bring concepts to life&#xa0;&#xa0;
Work closely with creatives and marketers to translate ideas into compelling motion visuals&#xa0;&#xa0;
Think beyond animation- focus on storytelling, product experience, and visual impact&#xa0;&#xa0;
Stay ahead of trends- explore new techniques in motion design, branding, and interactive visuals&#xa0;
Qualifications
Proven experience as a Motion Designer with a strong design-first approach and deep expertise in typography, color theory, and composition, demonstrated through impactful and complex projects.
Proficiency in Figma and Adobe applications (like Photoshop, Illustrator, and After Effects), familiarity with 3D workflows, and an openness to AI-enhanced design tools&#xa0;&#xa0;
A sharp eye for aesthetics-able to craft beautiful, effective, and brand-consistent motion work&#xa0;&#xa0;
Strong conceptual thinker-capable of ideating, sketching, and designing motion-based storytelling&#xa0;&#xa0;
Excellent communication skills in English, both written and spoken&#xa0;&#xa0;
Proactive and independent-takes initiative, adapts quickly, and leads motion design projects from start to finish&#xa0;
Additional Information
We're Base44, a newly acquired part of Wix, on a mission to change how software gets built. Our AI-powered platform empowers anyone to create custom software applications using natural language- no traditional coding required. Operating like a startup within Wix, we're fast, collaborative, and focused on turning complex problems into simple, powerful solutions.
We exist for creators, solo founders, startups, entrepreneurs, side hustlers, and everyone who wants to turn their ideas into reality. Whether you're launching a product, validating a concept, or exploring a hunch, Base44 helps you build it.
We're growing fast, the opportunity is huge, and with your help, our user-driven growth can become unstoppable.

Company Description
Job Description
We are seeking a highly accomplished AI Researcher to be part of the development of next-generation Foundation Models and Generative AI systems. In this role, you will bridge the gap between cutting-edge academic research and production-grade AI infrastructure. You will build, design, and fine-tune large-scale architectures (including LLMs, Multimodal, and Tabular Foundation Models) while applying them to complex, real-world domains like agentic behavior, coding and decision making.
In your day-to-day, you will:
Conduct pioneering research in deep learning and generative AI, specializing in Foundation Models, NLP, alignment, and multimodal learning&#xa0;&#xa0;
Deal with the impact of the models on production traffic, cost quality and latency
Train and scale state-of-the-art architectures using techniques like Post-Training SFT, Knowledge Distillation, LoRA, and sparse/hybrid model architectures&#xa0;&#xa0;
Own the AI lifecycle—from algorithmic prototyping and synthetic data generation to deploying production-grade AI features in fast-paced or big-data environments
Drive research initiatives, author publications/patents, and collaborate with other research teams to integrate intelligent capabilities into core products&#xa0;&#xa0;
Qualifications
5+ years of experience as a Research Scientist or Algorithm Developer within world-class AI labs or high-growth GenAI startups&#xa0;&#xa0;
Ph.D. or Master’s degree with honors in computer science, data science, statistics, or a highly quantitative field from a top-tier institution&#xa0;&#xa0;
Expert-level proficiency in PyTorch and deep learning training/inference optimization&#xa0;&#xa0;
Hands-on experience training, fine-tuning, or optimizing large-scale LLMs in research or production environments&#xa0;
Advanced programming skills in Python and/or C/C++ with experience in production-grade code and big data infrastructure&#xa0;&#xa0;
A portfolio of peer-reviewed publications in top-tier AI/ML venues or granted patents in advanced machine learning systems&#xa0;
Additional Information
We're Base44, a newly acquired part of Wix, on a mission to redefine how software is built. Our AI-powered platform enables anyone to create custom software applications using natural language—no coding required. Operating like a startup within Wix, we're fast, collaborative, and focused on solving complex problems with simple, powerful solutions.&#xa0;&#xa0;
We exist to empower creators, solo founders, startups, entrepreneurs, and side hustlers to bring their ideas to life. Whether you're launching a product, validating a concept, or exploring a new idea, Base44 is here to help you build it.&#xa0;&#xa0;
We're growing rapidly, the potential is immense, and with your expertise, we can drive user-driven growth to new heights.

