About the Role:
Kenes Group is looking for a motivated and creative Marketing Communications Intern to support our global Marketing Communications team.&#160;
This is a hands-on opportunity to gain experience across corporate communications, content creation, social media, employer branding, industry events, newsletter production, media relations, and digital marketing within a global&#160;organisation.&#160;
Working closely with the Marketing Communications Manager, you will help bring stories to life, support company-wide communications, create engaging content, and contribute to projects that promote the Kenes brand across multiple channels and audiences.&#160;
This is a 3-month&#160;hybrid&#160;internship, working full days Monday to Wednesday.
What You'll Be Doing:&#160;
Create and schedule content for social media, newsletters, website news, blogs, and internal communications&#160;
Design visuals in Canva and edit short-form videos and reels in&#160;CapCut&#160;
Support the production and promotion of the company newsletter&#160;
Maintain content calendars, asset libraries, and project trackers&#160;
Research industry trends, competitors, media opportunities, awards, and speaking opportunities&#160;
Support the Kenes Ambassadors&#160;programme&#160;and employer branding initiatives&#160;
Assist&#160;with communications around company events, conferences, milestones, and internal campaigns&#160;
Monitor social media performance and prepare basic reports&#160;
Gather information, statistics, and content from stakeholders across the business&#160;
Provide first drafts of content, creative assets, and communications materials for review&#160;
What We're Looking For:&#160;
Excellent written and spoken English&#160;
Strong attention to detail&#160;
Interest in communications, marketing, PR,&#160;journalism&#160;or content creation&#160;
Familiarity with social media platforms and digital trends&#160;
Basic experience with Canva (preferred, not mandatory)&#160;
Basic experience with&#160;CapCut&#160;or short-form video editing (preferred, not&#160;mandatory)&#160;
Strong&#160;organizational&#160;and time-management skills&#160;
Curious,&#160;proactive&#160;and eager to learn&#160;
Comfortable working independently and taking ownership of tasks&#160;
What You'll Learn:&#160;
By the end of the internship, you will have practical experience in:&#160;
Corporate communications&#160;
Content marketing&#160;
Social media management&#160;
Newsletter production&#160;
Employer branding&#160;
Media relations&#160;
Industry research and monitoring&#160;
Event communications&#160;
Canva design and visual storytelling&#160;
Video editing for digital channels&#160;
Working within an international business environment&#160;
&#160;
What Success Looks Like:&#160;
By the end of the internship, you will be able to:&#160;
Independently create first drafts of communication materials&#160;
Develop social media content aligned with brand guidelines&#160;
Produce Canva graphics and short-form videos with minimal supervision&#160;
Maintain content calendars and communication trackers&#160;
Conduct industry research and present actionable insights&#160;
Contribute meaningfully to ongoing communications campaigns and projects&#160;
Operate as a trusted member of the Marketing Communications team&#160;
WHAT WE OFFER:&#160;
Competitive salary and full-time labor contract.
Flexible benefits program: food vouchers, optional additional health insurance, corporate discounts, etc.
Fixed working hours (Monday-Friday).
Hybrid working mode, excellent office location, and free shuttle bus from the metro station to the office.
Gifts for special occasions, fruits, massages, and yoga classes in the office once per week.
Real opportunities for professional development in a leading international company.
Friendly team culture that promotes initial and continual professional education and team collaboration.
Regular team events.
Refer a friend program.
